// Chapter 1 — the camp. Shows a hub (@hub) whose options are storylets tagged "camp".
// flag:guide-doubtful starts true (see the mapping-form flags in story.talewright.yaml).

=== camp.arrival
@title Base Camp

{image("camp-art", "A riverside expedition camp with canvas tents and supplies at the edge of dense jungle.")}

The boat leaves {player:first-name} at the edge of the jungle with a pack, {item:torch#a#lower} and
three weeks of unanswered letters. The {faction:explorers-guild} has given {player:pronoun:object}
one season to find **{item:relic#the}** before they hand the expedition to someone more *reliable*.

> guide: {player:name}. You're later than your letter promised. I'm {guide:first-name} — the guild sent me.

{player:last-name#possessive} reputation for punctuality is, {player:pronoun} {player:pronoun#one-many("has", "have")} to admit, deserved.

-> camp.hub

=== camp.hub
@title The Camp
@hub camp

The camp hums with insects. {guide:first-name} sharpens a machete by the fire{if var:supplies > 0}, eyeing the supplies you bought{/if}.
{if flag:guide-doubtful}
{guide:pronoun#capitalize} hasn't said what {guide:pronoun} thinks of your chances. {guide:pronoun#capitalize} doesn't have to.
{else}
{guide:pronoun#capitalize} catches your eye and nods, as if the two of you have already agreed on something.
{/if}

* [Set out for the temple] -> trail.river

=== camp.supplies
@title Haggle for supplies
@tags camp
@once
@priority 10
@hub camp and records

{image("expedition-workshop", "A sheltered camp worktable holds a rucksack, rations, rope and expedition records beside a hanging watch bell.")}

A trader with a gold tooth unrolls a blanket of goods. You come away with a {item:rope#lower} and a
{item:charm#lower} he swears keeps the river spirits polite.
Two {item:ration}s complete the bargain. The trader sets the expedition register
beside your pack and points to the empty signature line.

~ give player rope
~ give player charm
~ give player ration 2
~ set flag:packing-open
~ var:supplies += 2

* [Return to camp] -> camp.hub

=== camp.register
@title Sign the expedition register
@tags camp,records
@once
@priority 10

The clerk writes **{player:name#upper}**, then carefully corrects the entry to
{player:name}. The margin says: "{player:pronoun#capitalize} signed
{player:pronoun:possessive-pronoun:determiner} own name; this copy is {player:pronoun:possessive-pronoun:independent}.
Ask {player:pronoun:object} to check it {player:pronoun:reflexive}."

{item:idol#a#capitalize} decorates the clerk's stamp. Its label reads \{expedition copy\}.
The clerk says {item:idol#this} {item:idol#one-many("belongs", "belong")} to the guild.

> guide: I use {guide:pronoun}/{guide:pronoun:object}. Names matter more than the guild admits.

-> camp.hub

=== camp.guide
@title What the Guild Never Wrote Down
@choice-label Ask **{guide:first-name}** about the temple
@tags camp
@once

> guide: The old ones built it to keep something *in*, not people out.
> The guild knows that. They never write it down.
>
> Last spring they sent {ines:name} up that stair. She came back talking only in numbers, and the guild filed her report under *weather*.
>
>
> I took this job expecting you to turn back at the river. You asked me first, though. Nobody from the guild has done that before.

{guide:first-name} spends the rest of the evening on the river crossing: where the current is slack, and where it only looks it.

{if faction:explorers-guild:tier >= friendly}
> guide: The guild speaks well of you. I'll do what I can.
{else}
> guide: Between us, the guild expects you to fail.
{/if}

~ faction:explorers-guild:standing += 5
~ clear flag:guide-doubtful
-> camp.hub

=== camp.journal
@title Study your journal
@tags camp
@once
@priority 5

You spread {player:pronoun:possessive-pronoun:determiner} {item:journal} across your knees. The glyph rubbings from the museum are smudged, but a pattern repeats: *a spiral, a closed eye, a hand.*

Beneath the last rubbing, the museum's copyist stepped the three signs down the page:

    *the spiral*
            *the closed eye*
                    *the hand*


Someone has written in the margin, very small: *in that order, and not before.*

* [Puzzle out the glyphs] skill-check history dc 12
  success: { set flag:knows-glyphs; player:xp += 50; player:lucidity += 2 } -> camp.journal-solved
  failure: -> camp.journal-failed

=== camp.journal-solved
It's a warning and an instruction at once: *close your eyes before the spiral, and the hand will open the way.*
You underline it twice. The pattern settles into focus; your Lucidity rises to **{player:lucidity}**.
-> camp.hub

=== camp.journal-failed
The marks blur into each other. You close the journal with a headache and nothing else.
-> camp.hub

// Text state: an explicit manifest default, a hoisted Talemark declaration, copied values,
// equality/inequality, empty text and literal assignments on choices.
=== camp.watchword
@title Agree on a night watchword
@tags camp
@once

~ var:watch-note = ""

> guide: If we lose each other after dark, call the watchword. Tonight's suggestion is "{var:watchword}".

{if var:watch-note == ""}
The watch ledger has no phrase recorded yet.
{/if}

* [Keep quiet river] -> camp.watchword-record
* [Use silver heron instead] { var:watchword = "silver heron" } -> camp.watchword-record

// Reply scenes continue the watchword conversation in the same passage; each is still its own
// history step. A continued scene has no @title or @clear.
=== camp.watchword-record
@continues

~ var:watch-note = var:watchword

You write **{var:watch-note}** in the watch ledger. {guide:first-name} asks what should happen if a stranger overhears it.

* [Change the watchword to lantern light] (requires var:watchword == var:watch-note) { var:watchword = "lantern light" } -> camp.watchword-readback
* [Retire the watchword without a replacement] (requires var:watchword == var:watch-note) { var:watchword = "" } -> camp.watchword-readback
* [Keep the recorded watchword] -> camp.watchword-readback

=== camp.watchword-readback
@continues

{if var:watchword == ""}
> guide: No watchword tonight, then. Stay within sight of the fire.
{else}
> guide: The current watchword is "{var:watchword}". Remember it, not the old one.
{/if}

{if var:watch-note != var:watchword}
The ledger still reads **{var:watch-note}**. Changing the spoken watchword did not rewrite the ink: the note holds a copy, not a promise to follow later changes.
{/if}

* [Close the watch ledger] -> camp.hub
